{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next sent only once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the previous one has a response or has failed."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record, then "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are the instrument’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"traceparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracestate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NoOpInstrument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the batch’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived. Any other status, or no response,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means it didn’t; either way the batch is not sent again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can still arrive twice: one a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" handles its own failures: a batch the encoder can’t encode, a send that gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no response and a response that isn’t 2xx are each logged at error level and dropped, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the delivery and its other destinations carry on. A cancelled delivery cancels the send in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flight, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns without logging it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L48","fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift"},"title":"HTTPDestination","roleHeading":"Structure"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as one request."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"t